# crontab.example - schedule for the nightly batch.
#
# Install for the current user with:  crontab -e   (then paste the line below,
# with the path changed to where the project lives)
#
# Fields: minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week command
#
# Runs at 01:30 every night. run_batch.sh writes its own timestamped log to
# data/logs/; cron.log only catches anything printed before logging starts
# (e.g. the log folder is unwritable). MAILTO, if the machine can send mail,
# emails that output to the support mailbox.
#
# MAILTO=vehicle-batch-support@example.org
30 1 * * * /path/to/vehicle-records-batch-processor/scripts/run_batch.sh >> /path/to/vehicle-records-batch-processor/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1
